1.6.1: page/engine version sentinel, real-DOM test harness

A half-cached deployment (browser serving the previous index.html while
re-fetching the new wasm and manifest) made the Print selector invisible
while the version label - which reports the engine - claimed the new
release. The page now carries its own PAGE_VERSION; on mismatch with
the engine it says so in the status line and tells the user to
hard-refresh, turning silent staleness into a labeled state. The
release script refuses to ship if PAGE_VERSION disagrees with VERSION.

scripts/test_page_dom.mjs runs the real page under jsdom - genuine
selects, optgroups and style semantics, where hand-rolled DOM stubs
have now been wrong three times - asserting boot, the print-selector
visibility contract in both directions, and film-dropdown leakage. It
skips cleanly when jsdom is not installed and runs in make check-wasm
otherwise.
